### What this PR does / why we need it?

Ascend NPU internal storage formats such as FRACTAL_NZ do not support the regular device-to-device `Tensor.copy_` path used by EPLB. Local expert staging and workspace commit can therefore fail with ERR01007 when expert weights use an internal format.

This PR:
- adds an Ascend-specific expert copy helper that validates tensor schema and NPU format;
- keeps `Tensor.copy_` for CPU and NPU ND tensors, and uses `torch_npu.copy_memory_` for matching internal-format tensors;
- routes local staging, workspace commit, and duplicate-expert copies through the helper;
- rejects mismatched NPU formats and non-zero-offset internal-format views with explicit errors.

This is the copy half of the EPLB fix. It complements #18015, which preserves the source NPU format when allocating EPLB buffers. No buffer-allocation changes are included here.

### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?

Yes. EPLB expert migration can copy Ascend internal-format weights without hitting the unsupported `copy_` path. There is no public API change.

### How was this patch tested?

Added unit coverage for:
- CPU and NPU ND fallback to `copy_`;
- internal-format NPU dispatch to `torch_npu.copy_memory_`;
- format mismatch and non-zero storage-offset rejection;
- primary and duplicate expert commits through the helper;
- explicit local EPLB staging through the helper;
- existing async EPLB workspace integration with the new module.

Static checks run locally:
- `ruff check` on all changed Python files;
- `ruff format --check` on all changed Python files;
- `git diff --check`.

The combined two-part fix (this PR plus #18015) was also exercised in the four-node EPLB deployment that originally reproduced the failure.

- vLLM main: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607

### What this PR does / why we need it?

Native block-wise FP8 checkpoints (`quant_method: "fp8"`) store E4M3 weights together with FP32 `weight_scale_inv` tensors. On pre-950 Ascend NPUs, some CANN builds cannot cast FP8 E4M3 weights to FP32 on device, so real checkpoint loading fails in `resolve_block_scales` before model forward.

This PR:

- resolves pre-950 NPU block-FP8 weights in bounded CPU FP32 chunks and transfers only the model-dtype result back to the NPU;
- keeps the existing device-side path on Ascend 950;
- marks an MLA `kv_b_proj` that has already been converted to BF16 as `AscendUnquantizedLinearMethod`, matching the MLA backend's execution-path type check;
- adds a focused unit assertion for the converted `kv_b_proj` method.

This is intentionally separated from the MRV2 fine-grained TP feature PR #16906. ModelSlim W8A8 checkpoints loaded with `--quantization ascend` do not use this native block-FP8 path.

### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?

Yes. Native block-wise FP8 checkpoints can be loaded on supported pre-950 Ascend NPUs even when the runtime cannot perform the E4M3-to-FP32 cast on device.

### How was this patch tested?

Checks on current `main` (`e139b7d57`):

- `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` for the implementation and focused UT file;
- `python -m py_compile` for both files;
- `git diff --check`;
- focused unit coverage verifies that the converted MLA `kv_b_proj` uses `AscendUnquantizedLinearMethod`.

Earlier A3 validation of the same implementation used a five-layer real DeepSeek-V3.1 subset containing native E4M3/`weight_scale_inv` tensors: all seven shards loaded, `/v1/models` returned HTTP 200, and an eight-token completion returned HTTP 200 with non-empty output. The exact rebased revision still requires the current CI/hardware rerun.
- vLLM main: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/84030bbe3d74d99bad477a3d2e37a973ccd8865c

### What this PR does / why we need it?

ModelRunnerV1 already supports DSV3.1 fine-grained Embedding TP and dense MLP TP, but MRV2 eager DP ranks can execute different token counts while these features reuse DP ranks as TP collectives. Different leading dimensions across the group can break the all-gather/reduce-scatter contract.

This PR:

- reuses MRV2's synchronized DP token vector and aligns eager batch descriptors to the group maximum only when Embedding TP or MLP TP is enabled;
- represents additional tokens as query-only padding, keeps KV/request-shaped buffers bounded, and clears the reusable padding mask between steps;
- composes FineTP alignment with the latest PCP+DP dispatch context from #16853 and preserves adaptive-verification query boundaries;
- removes the recompute-scheduler requirement for MRV2 Embedding TP while preserving the MRV1 and o_proj gates;
- restores FULL_DECODE_ONLY/FULL_AND_PIECEWISE eligibility only for the one-token PD decode-recompute handoff.

The feature-disabled path is unchanged. This implementation-only commit excludes UT, E2E scripts, and documentation. The native block-FP8 loader fix is now isolated in #16922. ModelSlim W8A8 checkpoints loaded with `--quantization ascend` do not use that path.

### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?

Yes. Deployments that explicitly enable ModelRunnerV2 can use fine-grained Embedding TP and MLP TP independently or together. ModelRunnerV1 behavior is unchanged.

### How was this patch tested?

Checks on current `main` (`e139b7d57`):

- `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` on both implementation files;
- `python -m py_compile` on both implementation files;
- `git diff --check`;
- conflict review against the latest PCP+DP implementation, confirming one combined `gather_batch_req_state` and nested PCP/FineTP dispatch contexts.

Earlier A3 validation of the FineTP implementation included:

- five-layer real DSV3.1 MRV2 OFF / Embedding TP8 / MLP TP8 / both;
- 20/20 functional graph matrix across NONE, PIECEWISE, FULL_DECODE_ONLY, FULL_AND_PIECEWISE, and requested FULL (resolved to FDO by MLA);
- per-chip model-memory reductions matching theory: Embedding TP8 1.51 GiB, MLP TP8 1.94 GiB, both 3.45 GiB;
- all-gather/reduce-scatter evidence on all ranks;
- single-node 8+8 P/D validation where remote KV transfer succeeded and all eight D ranks replayed `run_fullgraph(num_tokens=1)`.

The exact rebased revision still needs the planned rerun with `/mnt/weight/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-w8a8-mtp` and `/mnt/weight/GLM-5.2-w8a8`. Direct server inspection confirmed both are ModelSlim W8A8/W8A8_DYNAMIC checkpoints containing I8 weights plus `weight_scale`/`weight_offset`, with zero `weight_scale_inv` tensors, so they do not depend on #16922.

The BF16 logits comparison keeps the same greedy token and top-20 set, but the original strict elementwise `atol=rtol=1e-2` gate remains a documented limitation (`max_abs=0.0625`).

- vLLM main: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/84030bbe3d74d99bad477a3d2e37a973ccd8865c
